# Build context for infra/docker/Dockerfile.node and Dockerfile.web (docker-bake.hcl, context ".").
# The images install their own dependencies for Linux, so nothing host-built may leak in: a Windows
# node_modules would carry win32 native bindings, and .next or dist would mask a stale build.

**/node_modules
**/.next
**/dist
**/.turbo
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/next-env.d.ts
out
build

# Secrets never enter an image or the build cache.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Not read by any image build. Both Dockerfiles `COPY . .` before bundling, so a file here that changes
# (k6 results and the invariants report are rewritten by every load run and `verify:invariants`) would
# invalidate that layer and rerun tsup and `next build` with no source change. tests/ holds no manifest.
.git
.github
.vscode
.idea
docs
tests
invariants-report.json
coverage
playwright-report
test-results
blob-report
uploads
**/*.log
CLAUDE*.md
